n mcut finds no fragment, do_boolean keeps the part it could not cut, so the accumulated mesh comes out exactly as it went in - the run reports success, the object is replaced by the result, the negative volume is gone and its cut is missing, with no error and no toast. That is the owner's symptom (and the same behaviour MB-1 found inside the gizmo). Fix: mcut::do_boolean now RETURNS whether it changed the mesh (the one place that knows; callers ignoring it are unaffected); csg::DifferenceReport counts the Difference parts asked for and how many changed nothing, including a Difference dropped because the accumulated mesh or the part's kernel mesh was missing (equally silent); perform_csgmesh_booleans_mcut(range, report) fills it; Plater::combine_mesh_fff passes the report, fills a Plater::ObjectBooleanReport for its caller, notifies the user through the same error channel the failure path uses and logs the reason at info (so it lands in %APPDATA%/OrcaSlicer/log and get_log_tail); the fallback path logs too. ObjectList::boolean() returns the report (menu ignores it) and the new MCP tool boolean_parts runs this exact path (it selects the object in the Object list, which is what boolean() reads) reporting objects/volumes/triangles before and after plus negative_parts / negative_parts_not_subtracted / boolean_failed / message. Verified: unit case (a 20mm cube Union + a 4mm cube Difference 100mm away -> offered 1, not_applied 1, body volume unchanged; centred -> not_applied 0, cavity 7936 = 20^3-4^3); [MeshBoolean] 3 cases / 17 assertions; ctest 2415/2415; runtime boolean_parts on a duplicate of the owner's object -> 29540 -> 42072 triangles, volumes 2 -> 1, negative_parts 1, not_subtracted 0, failed false, i.e. the right-click path cuts the hole correctly on the state they left. Their earlier failure was not reproduced on that state and the CGAL gate never logged a refusal in the recent sessions, so the cause of that specific run is unknown; what is certain now is that 